<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech 1996 wheat harvest seen dipping - stats bureau.</title>
<headline>Czech 1996 wheat harvest seen dipping - stats bureau.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Statistical Bureau on Monday estimated the 1996 total wheat harvest at 3.629 million tonnes compared with 3.822 million tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>The figures were revised slightly downward from a July forecast of 3.648 million due to marginally lower-than expected yield on fewer hectares sown.</p>
<p>Agriculture ministry officials have said recently that the harvest should still meet the country's grain demand, and there is a possibility of surplus exports.  </p>
<p> CZECH HARVEST		1996	   1996	  1995</p>
<p>				(AUG-est)   (JULY-est)</p>
<p> winter wheat (million tonnes)3.461	  3.477	 3.693</p>
<p> spring wheat		 0.168	  0.171	 0.130</p>
<p>   total wheat		3.629	  3.648	 3.823</p>
<p>avg yield (tonnes/hectare)</p>
<p> winter wheat		  4.58	   4.60	  4.65</p>
<p> spring wheat		  3.76	   3.81	  3.59</p>
<p>   total wheat		 4.53	   4.55	  4.60</p>
<p>hectares sown (actual)</p>
<p> winter wheat	     756,484	   n/a	 794,647</p>
<p> spring wheat		44,855	   n/a	  36,106</p>
<p>   total		    801,339	   n/a	 830,753</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
